<title>UK: MARKETS-BRITAIN-SHARES.</title>
<headline>MARKETS-BRITAIN-SHARES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's FTSE 100 stock index scaled new heights on Friday, clambering above the 4,200 level for the first time after the Dow reached another closing high overnight and British interest rates remained on hold.</p>
<p>By 0913 GMT the FTSE 100 index of British blue-chip stocks was up 2.8 points at 4,200.3, surpassing the previous record of 4,198.9 set on Thursday.</p>
